course: dictionary
lesson: 6266
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The monarch waved from the balcony to the crowds.» A balcony and crowds suggest a royal ruler, so monarch means a king or queen here.
explain: Read the words around it: «Monarch caterpillars eat milkweed.» Caterpillars and milkweed are about nature, so monarch here means the orange-and-black butterfly. Ask yourself: what kind of thing is this sentence about?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well. Swapping «king» into the caterpillar sentence breaks it, so the clues point to the butterfly.
fact: A monarch is a king or queen, or an emperor or empress, who rules a country.
fact: Most monarchs are born into the royal family, so they become ruler without being elected.
fact: «Queen Elizabeth II reigned for 70 years, from 1952 to 2022» means she ruled as monarch for 70 years.
fact: A monarch butterfly is large, orange and black, and lives in North America.
fact: A country ruled by a monarch is called a monarchy.
exercise: «The British monarch is also head of state of 14 other Commonwealth countries.» Who is the monarch in this sentence? | *A king or queen who rules Britain | A butterfly from Canada | A kind of poisonous milkweed | A bird that avoids orange butterflies
exercise: «Monarch butterflies fly thousands of kilometres to mountains in Mexico for winter.» What is a monarch in this sentence? | A mountain in Mexico | A country with a royal family | *A large orange-and-black butterfly | A king or queen
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Monarch caterpillars eat milkweed, and birds learn to avoid them.» that is a kind of plant. | avoid | monarch | caterpillars | *milkweed
test: «Monarchs taste bad to birds because their caterpillars eat poisonous milkweed.» Which meaning of monarch is this? | *A butterfly | A country with a royal family | A king or queen | A poison
test: What is a monarchy? | *A country ruled by a king or queen | A large butterfly that flies to Mexico | A type of milkweed | A royal palace with gardens
exam: Jayden reads «The monarch was born into a royal family and ruled for 40 years.» What does monarch mean? | *A king or queen who rules a country | A poisonous plant | A bird that avoids orange butterflies | A butterfly that flies to Mexico
